# Requests to try the sample by hand: run it with `dotnet run`, then send them from
# Visual Studio, Rider or Visual Studio Code with the REST Client extension.

@host = http://localhost:5000

### A valid invoice: the identifiers come back without presentation characters.
POST {{host}}/invoices
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "supplier": "BE 0202.239.951",
  "account": "BE68 5390 0754 7034",
  "reference": "+++123/4567/89002+++"
}

### Three invalid fields, reported at once with their codes, in French.
POST {{host}}/invoices
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: fr-BE

{
  "supplier": "0202.239.952",
  "account": "NL91 ABNA 0417 1643 00"
}

### The same, in Dutch.
POST {{host}}/invoices
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: nl-BE

{
  "supplier": "0202.239.952",
  "account": "NL91 ABNA 0417 1643 00"
}

### An enterprise number bound from the route.
GET {{host}}/enterprise-numbers/BE0202239951

### An invalid enterprise number in the route: a plain 400, without the reason.
GET {{host}}/enterprise-numbers/0202.239.952

### Two business days after Thursday 2 April 2026: Easter Monday is skipped.
GET {{host}}/business-days?from=2026-04-02&days=2

### Ten business days before 5 January 2026.
GET {{host}}/business-days?from=2026-01-05&days=-10
